{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Primordial Blast rank 502825 comes back from an Elemental Mastery transform without a New Spell Learned toast (#7515, #7723)",
  "contract": "#7515 and #7723 report a 'learned Primordial Blast' pop-up each time an Elemental Mastery or Runic Brand transform of Primordial Blast 502825 ends, on a level 38-40 Spiritmage. Both reports came from builds before #7765, which mutes the swap back: SetTemporarySpellReplacement swaps the bars with SMSG_SUPERCEDED_SPELL and the client draws the toast when the swapped-in spell's SpellCustomAttr row carries 0x400. 502825 has no row in the client's own table; mod-spellbook pushes it one (59107) with the bit set when the spell is taught. The transformed spells keep their client rows (712668 row 23389), which lack the bit, so swapping them in is silent. The reported rank, at the reported level, must come back muted both when the transform expires and when its cast consumes it, with no learned-spell packet, and stay notable for a genuine learn.",
  "timeout_ms": 90000,
